course: dictionary
lesson: 1039
title: Borderland
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A border is the line between two countries or regions. Land is ground. Put them together and you get borderland: the land near that line. «Cossacks appeared in the steppe borderlands» tells you they lived on land close to a border, not in the middle of a country.
explain: Read the clues after the word. «They fished, hunted and fought Tatar raiders.» People who fish and hunt need to live on the land, and people who fight raiders are fighting for safety. So the borderlands were not calm, quiet places. Ask: what kind of place needs people to fight? Then check your meaning in the sentence.
explain: Borderland can also be an idea, not a place. «The borderland between sleep and waking» is the strange, foggy time when you are not fully asleep and not fully awake. It is a state between two things, and it is not clearly one or the other.
fact: A border is a line between two countries or regions.
fact: «Borderland» means the land near a border between two countries or regions.
fact: «Borderland» can also mean a state or area between two things that is not clearly one or the other.
fact: The Scottish Borders were borderlands where raids and battles happened in history.
fact: In stories, a borderland is often wild and dangerous.
exercise: «Cossacks appeared in the steppe borderlands.» What is a borderland? | *The land near the border between two countries or regions | A kind of boat used for fishing | A type of horse | A big city in the middle of a desert
exercise: «They fished, hunted and fought Tatar raiders.» Which word shows the borderlands could be dangerous? | fished | served | hunted | *fought
exercise: «The borderland between sleep and waking.» What does this mean? | *A state between two things, not clearly asleep or awake | A deep sleep with no dreams at all | A long walk to school in the morning | A bed with a soft pillow
test: The dusk, when the sun has set but it is not yet dark, is a kind of borderland between day and night. What does this mean? | A bright lamp in a room | Midnight, when every light is off | *A time that is neither fully day nor fully night | Noon, when the sun is highest
test: Which sentence uses borderland to mean land near a border? | The borderland of the football pitch is painted white. | The borderland of my bedroom is full of toys. | I felt a borderland of sadness after the film. | *Our village sits in the borderlands, close to the line between the two countries.
exam: «Cossacks ... fished, hunted and fought Tatar raiders» in the steppe borderlands; from this context, what kind of place were the borderlands? | A quiet park with benches and swings | A school for musicians | A shop full of food and drink | *A wild, dangerous place where people had to fight and survive
